{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "DKyiGoUNIM", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-22", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 905450, "segment_id": "FDqHtnYxSM", "segment_broadcast_id": "DKyiGoUNIM", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Charles Gibson (New York)", "segment_description": null, "segment_duration": 60, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 905450, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "DKyiGoUNIM", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-22", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 905450, "segment_id": "UetLhTl5SW", "segment_broadcast_id": "DKyiGoUNIM", "segment_title": "Economy: Bailout Package", "segment_description": "(Studio: Charles Gibson)  The jitters on Wall Street over the proposed government bailout plan noted; Stock Market Report and oil price figures cited.  \n\n(Capitol Hill: Jake Tapper)  The hurdles to an agreement on the bailout deal examined; details given about the sticking points in the aid package: bankruptcy reform and executive compensation.  [On \"This Week,\" Treasury Secretary Henry PAULSON&nbsp- says we need this {bill} quick.]  [Senators John McCAIN, Barack OBAMA&nbsp- question giving a blank check to Washington.]  [Representative Frank LUCAS&#134;- comments on the compensation issue.]  [On Fox News, PAULSON&nbsp- says it cannot be punitive.]  [Representative Barney FRANK&nbsp- comments on the reaction.]  \n\n(Studio: Betsy Stark)  The skeptical reaction on Wall Street to the bailout plan and to the jump in the price of oil examined; details given of the announcement by Goldman Sachs and MorganStanley they are remaking themselves as commercial banks.  [Charles Schwab investment officer Liz Ann SONDERS&#134;, Egan-Jones analyst Sean EGAN&#134;- comment on the economic situation.]  [\"Wall Street: A History\" author Charles GEISST&#134;- reacts to the banks changing their business model.]  The likelihood of the continuing of manic behavior by Wall Street until the bailout deal is worked out noted.  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson; Washington: George Stephanopoulos)  The issues still to be resolved in the bailout plan, the question of will there be relief for people in mortgage trouble and how the politics of the situation will effect the two presidential candidates discussed. ", "segment_duration": 390, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63060.0", "legacy_segment_id": 905451, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "DKyiGoUNIM", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-22", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 905450, "segment_id": "QrMbaWCppR", "segment_broadcast_id": "DKyiGoUNIM", "segment_title": "Campaign 2008 / Obama vs. McCain / Virginia", "segment_description": "(Studio: Charles Gibson)  The standings of Senators Barack Obama and John McCain in a new ABC News/\"Washington Post\" poll of the state of Virginia cited.   (Virginia Beach: John Berman)  The race in Virginia featured; scenes shown from an Obama field office in Williamsburg, Virginia and of neighbors meeting neighbors; details given about the politics of the state.  [Obama Virginia director Mitch STEWART&#134;, Virginia professor Larry SABATO&#134;- offer views on the Obama organization in Virginia.]  [REPUBLICAN&nbsp- comments on the effect of Governor Sarah Palin.] ", "segment_duration": 130, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63450.0", "legacy_segment_id": 905452, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "DKyiGoUNIM", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-22", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 905450, "segment_id": "F0dgGgqFLP", "segment_broadcast_id": "DKyiGoUNIM", "segment_title": "Pakistan / Islamabad Hotel Bombing", "segment_description": "(Studio: Charles Gibson)  Report introduced.   (Islamabad: Jim Sciutto)  The massive truck bomb attack Saturday on the Marriott hotel in Islamabad, Pakistan, featured; scenes shown of the burned-out hotel, the wreckage inside, hotel video of the truck at the gate, the crater site and the wounded; details given of Pakistan's confusion over how to deal with militants.  [Marriott Islamabad owner Sadruddin HASHWANI&#134;- says security was breached.]  [Retired Lt. Gen. Talat MASOOD&#134;- cites the government's problems in dealing with this with US involvement.] ", "segment_duration": 140, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63580.0", "legacy_segment_id": 905453, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "DKyiGoUNIM", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-22", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broa